# Line endings in the files that the tests read.
#
# Several tests compare a rendered block of text against an expected block of
# text. A Windows checkout converts a text file to CRLF by default, and that
# conversion changes the bytes. The test then fails in a way that looks like a
# defect in a renderer rather than a setting in the checkout.
#
# Pin the text files to LF on every platform. This is not a preference about
# editors. It is the condition under which the tests mean anything on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf

# Binary, and never converted.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff2 binary
